--TEST--
A destructuring leaf is an element read, so it takes a subscript's own refusals — `E0482` for a value with no elements, `E0401` for an element type the leaf does not declare, and `E0483` for a leaf that would alias what it read — `rule:types/grammar`.3 and 5, `rule:types/implicit-capture`
--FILE--
<?nvs
array<int> $pair = [1, 2];
// The element type is checked against what the leaf declares, in the
// same direction and with the same covariance a `foreach` value binding
// gets: an `int` element does not satisfy a `string` binding.
[string $wrong] = $pair;
// `rule:types/implicit-capture` removed by-reference capture and `rule:classes/two-copy-depths` makes an
// element a copy, so a leaf that aliased the entry it was read from
// would have no owner in either rule — the array literal's own `&value`
// refusal, arrived at from the other side.
[inout int $aliased] = $pair;
// Destructuring reads elements, so a value that names no element type
// has nothing to take apart. This is `E0482`'s rule verbatim, which is
// why it is `E0482`'s code.
[int $notAnArray] = 7;
// A `mixed` is the same answer for the same reason: `rule:types/conversion` makes
// it the one unchecked position, and an unchecked position names no
// element type either.
mixed $anything = 5;
[int $fromMixed] = $anything;
// A nested target is checked against the element it takes apart, at
// every depth.
array<array<int>> $nest = [[1]];
[[string $deep]] = $nest;
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `int`
  --> %s:6:2
  |
6 | [string $wrong] = $pair;
  |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `int`

error[E0483]: a destructuring leaf cannot bind by reference
   --> %s:11:2
   |
11 | [inout int $aliased] = $pair;
   |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this would alias the element it was read from
   = help: drop the `inout` — the leaf is a copy, exactly as an array literal's element is; to share one mutable cell, put it in an object (`rule:types/implicit-capture`)

error[E0482]: cannot destructure `int`
   --> %s:15:21
   |
15 | [int $notAnArray] = 7;
   |                     ^ this is `int`
   = help: destructuring reads elements out of an `array<T>` — declare one, or read the value out by hand

error[E0482]: cannot destructure `mixed`
   --> %s:20:20
   |
20 | [int $fromMixed] = $anything;
   |                    ^^^^^^^^^ this is `mixed`
   = help: destructuring reads elements out of an `array<T>` — declare one, or read the value out by hand

error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `int`
   --> %s:24:3
   |
24 | [[string $deep]] = $nest;
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `int`

error: aborting due to 5 errors
